{%- comment -%}
  Reader comments via giscus (github.com/giscus/giscus), backed by GitHub Discussions on
  {{ site.giscus.repo }}. One-time setup before this renders real comments:
    1. Make sure the repo is public.
    2. Repo Settings -> General -> Features -> enable "Discussions".
    3. Install the giscus app (https://github.com/apps/giscus) and grant it access to the repo.
    4. Go to https://giscus.app, fill in the repo, pick the "{{ site.giscus.category }}" category
       and "pathname" mapping, then copy the generated data-repo-id / data-category-id from the
       snippet at the bottom of the page. Use "General", not "Announcements" — giscus currently
       can't create new discussions in an Announcement-type category (see site.giscus's comment
       in src/_data/site.js for details).
    5. Paste those into site.giscus.repoId / site.giscus.categoryId in src/_data/site.js.
  Theme starts as our own custom light theme (src/assets/giscus-themes/light.css — matches this
  site's monochrome palette instead of giscus's default GitHub colors, e.g. the green "Comment"
  button); giscus-theme-sync.js swaps to dark.css to match the site's active theme (and keeps it
  in sync with the theme-toggle button) once the widget's iframe has loaded.
{%- endcomment -%}
<section class="post__comments" id="comments">
  <h2 class="post__comments-title">Comments</h2>
  <script
    src="https://giscus.app/client.js"
    data-repo="{{ site.giscus.repo }}"
    data-repo-id="{{ site.giscus.repoId }}"
    data-category="{{ site.giscus.category }}"
    data-category-id="{{ site.giscus.categoryId }}"
    data-mapping="pathname"
    data-strict="0"
    data-reactions-enabled="1"
    data-emit-metadata="0"
    data-input-position="top"
    data-theme="{{ site.url }}/assets/giscus-themes/light.css"
    data-lang="en"
    data-loading="lazy"
    crossorigin="anonymous"
    async
  ></script>
</section>
